WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.720
So Joe Biden recently put out his climate
change plan and clean energy plan, and he

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.361
gave really a pretty solid speech about it.

00:00:07.361 --> 00:00:13.610
And I think it's important to cover this stuff
because no one trumps not really doing policy.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:20.080
And I do think it's important to draw a contrast
when one candidate is calling an urgent press

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.940
conference at the White House and spending
52 minutes.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:30.270
I believe it was sort of a radically misreading
attacks on Joe Biden from a piece of paper,

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:33.360
whereas Joe Biden is actually doing policy.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.610
Now, I know that some people in my audience
are going to be furious with me.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:42.460
How dare I say that Joe Biden's climate change
proposal is pretty good.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.480
It's not the Green New Deal.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.079
It's not Bernie's plan.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:49.230
It's not AOSIS plan or whatever the case may
be.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.700
You know what?

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.460
Let let let's analyze it critically and understand
what have been the climate change policies

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.809
of people who have been presidents.

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:05.880
And by that standard, this is the most progressive
climate change proposal that if Biden is elected,

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.249
would ever be associated with a sitting president.

00:01:09.249 --> 00:01:14.890
Of course, you can find people who have run,
who have had other proposals which we might

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:17.340
like better, and I'm including myself in that
list.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:24.310
But if Biden gets elected, this would be the
climate change proposal most to the left of

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:25.749
any previous president.

00:01:25.749 --> 00:01:27.979
And that's, I think, a really important thing
to keep in mind.

00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:33.049
So we're taking a break from the nonsense
and the insults and the hyperbole and the

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:35.350
bragging of Donald Trump.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:40.409
And I need to do a better job of when Joe
Biden talks about policy and puts out proposals.

00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:41.679
I should talk about it.

00:01:41.679 --> 00:01:46.409
Last time I did this, I went into some detail
about Joe Biden's tax plan.

00:01:46.409 --> 00:01:47.409
It's pretty solid.

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:51.469
It does a number of important things that
progressives should be happy about.

00:01:51.469 --> 00:01:55.130
Despite Biden's reputation as not being particularly
progressive.

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:59.189
And so I'm not going to redo the whole tax
plan story.

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:03.969
But Joe Biden's tax plan includes a number
of important provisions, like removing the

00:02:03.969 --> 00:02:07.789
cap on Social Security tax above 400000 a
year in earnings.

00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:12.360
That raises a huge amount of money from people
earning above four hundred thousand dollars

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.540
a year.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:19.000
Biden would propose or proposes eliminating
the stepped up basis provision for inheritances.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.151
I explain that last time.

00:02:20.151 --> 00:02:23.599
I mean, this is really significant stuff in
terms of the money it would raise.

00:02:23.599 --> 00:02:29.120
I won't redo the entire tax segment, but needless
to say, many in the audience appreciated it.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.379
Some just came in and said it's not as progressive
as what Bernie wanted.

00:02:32.379 --> 00:02:37.459
OK, let's now look at Joe Biden's proposal
on environmental justice and climate change

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:38.459
and clean energy.

00:02:38.459 --> 00:02:44.390
Now, off the bat, there's a bunch of sort
of regular regulatory stuff in the proposal,

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:46.280
which I'm not going to spend a lot of time
on.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:51.970
But it it does bear mentioning, which includes
Biden would establish an environmental climate

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:55.260
justice division in the Department of Justice.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:03:01.580
Biden would make environmental justice a priority
within the federal government.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:07.120
Biden would refresh the way that and to rehash
the way that the EPA does compliance.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.159
That stuff deserves attention.

00:03:09.159 --> 00:03:14.269
But I want to look at some of the specific
metrics and actions that Joe Biden has included

00:03:14.269 --> 00:03:15.269
in his plan.

00:03:15.269 --> 00:03:21.749
So, for example, Joe Biden includes specific
water quality improvements just to pick one

00:03:21.749 --> 00:03:23.909
thing that's in his climate plan.

00:03:23.909 --> 00:03:29.870
And if you look at this part of the plan,
Biden actually discusses and addresses specific

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:34.090
chemicals that are too much in our drinking
water.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:39.220
And he does it in a way where he sees water
not only as an environmental issue, which

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:43.230
it is, but also as an economic issue, which
it is.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:46.989
He sees water as an issue of social justice
as well.

00:03:46.989 --> 00:03:54.739
So I think we should all be pleased that Joe
Biden is talking about water quality in his

00:03:54.739 --> 00:04:02.889
environmental proposal in a way that shows
understanding of how water relates to race,

00:04:02.889 --> 00:04:08.109
class, geography, economics, et cetera, et
cetera.

00:04:08.109 --> 00:04:13.879
Remember, Joe Biden said that he would use
the Green New Deal as a framework in thinking

00:04:13.879 --> 00:04:16.359
about what he wants to do.

00:04:16.359 --> 00:04:21.001
And you can identify many things in his climate
change and clean energy proposals that are

00:04:21.001 --> 00:04:23.229
almost verbatim from the Green New Deal.

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:29.300
Now, what's hilarious is when Biden put this
out and people identified, look, this is like

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.370
straight out of Bernie's plan.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.580
This is straight out of green New Deal.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:38.669
There were people who previously were criticizing
Biden for not being progressive enough, who

00:04:38.669 --> 00:04:43.620
now are saying, oh, look, Biden copied stuff
from Bernie in the Green New Deal.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:48.800
Shouldn't we be glad to see Biden adopting
things from Bernie Sanders and from the Green

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:49.800
New Deal?

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:53.810
Like if the concern was that Biden wasn't
taking the Green New Deal seriously enough?

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:57.770
Shouldn't we be glad to see elements of the
green New Deal in Biden's proposal?

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.419
And you can see these.

00:04:59.419 --> 00:05:01.199
Components in a few different areas.

00:05:01.199 --> 00:05:07.069
When you look at Biden's plan for retrofitting
buildings and schools in a way that will be

00:05:07.069 --> 00:05:11.129
good for the environment but economically
stimulative.

00:05:11.129 --> 00:05:12.900
That's straight out of the green New Deal.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:17.729
A lot of the other things Biden includes in
these proposals are pretty obvious things,

00:05:17.729 --> 00:05:20.910
but they're things that aren't being done
or or at least not done enough.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:26.030
Like, for example, more seriously putting
in place subsidies and rebates when Americans

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:32.280
upgrade to more efficient sources of energy
and better windows and efficient appliances.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.370
That's worthwhile government spending.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:39.849
Now, two days ago, Donald Trump attacked Joe
Biden for having an ambitious goal in his

00:05:39.849 --> 00:05:40.849
proposal.

00:05:40.849 --> 00:05:49.320
And the goal is Biden wants to be carbon to
carbon pollution free electricity by 2035,

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:51.039
meaning by 2035.

00:05:51.039 --> 00:05:57.750
Biden wants the country to be generating electricity
from sources that do not pollute.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:01.520
From the standpoint of carbon, that's a huge
task.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:07.610
But if the criticism here is that Biden is
too ambitious on climate and clean energy,

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:08.610
I'll take it.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:12.770
I mean, look at the Trump administration that's
going in the opposite direction, wanting to

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:18.250
loosen emission standards for vehicles, wanting
to rehabilitate coal.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:20.620
We've had that for three and a half years.

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:24.800
I'll take an overly ambitious proposal from
Joe Biden any day.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:31.330
And importantly, one of the things I like
about this proposal, again, is Joe Biden is

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:36.349
connecting energy issues to economics and
social justice and race.

00:06:36.349 --> 00:06:41.159
And he's connecting environmental issues to
all of those same areas.

00:06:41.159 --> 00:06:46.990
So, for example, when Biden talks about his
proposal that by 2035 he wants to be generate

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:49.800
generating electricity from sources that don't
pollute.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:56.729
From the standpoint of carbon, he specifically
says, let's do this by creating jobs with

00:06:56.729 --> 00:07:02.360
this green energy shift where we will look
to HPC, use historically black colleges and

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:06.199
universities for training and hiring, et cetera.

00:07:06.199 --> 00:07:07.900
Just one example.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:13.530
So where I'm ending up on this is if you know
something about Joe Biden, you actually shouldn't

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:16.819
be surprised that his climate and energy proposal
is very solid.

00:07:16.819 --> 00:07:22.080
Joe Biden actually wrote the first climate
change mitigation bill in 1987.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.000
He tried it in 86 and it went nowhere in 87.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.770
It was signed into law by President Ronald
Reagan.

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:33.720
And it's particularly disappointing to see
some leftists who are framing Joe Biden as

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:38.090
kind of like reluctantly dealing with climate
change, sort of.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.629
Biden actually has been on this for more than
30 years.

00:07:40.629 --> 00:07:44.360
There's lots of areas where Biden has not
really been great unless you look at the last

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.360
10 years.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:48.310
If you look 25 years ago, there's areas where
Biden was not so good.

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:50.610
Biden has been on climate for more than 30
years.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:55.050
He said he would use the Green New Deal as
a framework for his proposal, and he did.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:58.509
So let's criticize Biden where it's warranted.

00:07:58.509 --> 00:08:02.909
Let's criticize Biden, where the proposals
he makes don't go far enough.

00:08:02.909 --> 00:08:06.400
And I'll be digging into that in more detail
probably next week.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:11.520
But know the pretending that Biden is just
a center right guy on every issue, including

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:12.520
climate.

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:13.659
It's wrong.

00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:19.000
And the fact that Biden put out this proposal
reinforces the importance of trying to take

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:23.819
the Senate so that we can maybe actually get
some of these things on Joe Biden's desk,

00:08:23.819 --> 00:08:28.280
put him in a position to have to sign stuff
into law rather than having this long list

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:32.030
of proposals that will never see the light
of day because Democrats don't control the

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.030
Senate anyway.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.170
So for me, it's reinforcing.

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:37.740
Hey, Biden's actually been pretty good on
climate for a long time.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:42.470
And number two, importantly, the importance
of the Senate to actually get some of this

00:08:42.470 --> 00:09:55.400
stuff in front of Joe Biden

00:09:55.400 --> 00:10:09.780
to sign.

